  "worked_solution": "Let's examine our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. Indeed, since \n\n$$\n0.55>0.5,\n$$\n\nmore than half of Olivia's performances were solos.\n\n- Statement II is false. Notice that \n\n$$\n40%<50%.\n$$\n\nSo, less than half of Harper's performances were solos.\n\n- Statement III is true. We can compare $0.55$ and $40%$ by converting the decimal into a percent. \n\nTo do this, we multiply it by $100:$\n\n$$\n0.55\\times 100=55%\n$$\n\nSince $55%>40%,$ Olivia had a **greater** percentage of solo performances compared to Harper.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only\".",
